# Material Design 3 (Jetpack Compose)

This app is **Material 3 only**. Use `androidx.compose.material3`. Material Icons (`androidx.compose.material.icons`) are allowed. Never import `androidx.compose.material` (M2).

Adapt to existing UI. Do not invent a parallel design system.

## Theme tokens

- Wrap new UI in `CarExpenseTrackerTheme`.
- Colors: `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` (wired in `Theme.kt` from `DesignTokens.Palette`). Do not hardcode `Color(0x…)` in screens.
- Exception: event semantic colors (`DesignTokens.Palette.fuel` / `repair` / `papers`) via `EventTypeBadge`.
- Type: `MaterialTheme.typography` (`labelMedium`, `bodyMedium`, `titleMedium`, `headlineSmall`).
- Space: `DesignTokens.Spacing` (`xs` 4, `sm` 8, `md` 16, `lg` 24, `xl` 32). No one-off `N.dp` padding.
- Honor `isSystemInDarkTheme()`. If you add a color, add it to **both** light and dark schemes in `Theme.kt`.

```kotlin
// BAD
Text("Monthly", color = Color(0xFF6B7280), fontSize = 12.sp)

// GOOD
Text("Monthly", style = MaterialTheme.typography.labelMedium, color = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.onSurfaceVariant)
```

## Components — reuse first

Prefer existing helpers in `ui/components/Components.kt`: `AppScreen`, `AppCard`, `MetricCard`, `PrimaryButton`, `SecondaryButton`, `SectionHeader`, `EmptyStateCard`, `CarHeader`, `EventTypeBadge`.

When building new UI, use M3 as-is: `Scaffold`, `NavigationBar`, `Card`, `Button`, `OutlinedButton`, `FilterChip`, `OutlinedTextField`, `ListItem`, `Icon`, `SnackbarHost`. Do not wrap them unless the same pattern already exists.

- Primary form/screen action: filled `Button` / `PrimaryButton`.
- Secondary: `OutlinedButton` / `SecondaryButton`.
- Destructive: `ButtonDefaults.buttonColors(containerColor = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.error)`.
- Filters: `FilterChip`, not custom tabs.
- Lists of settings/actions: `ListItem`.
- Empty data: `EmptyStateCard`.
- Bottom nav already lives in `AppNavHost` — do not add a second bar.

## Layout and a11y

- Screens with app bar / FAB / snackbar use `Scaffold` and consume its `padding`.
- Icon-only controls need `contentDescription` (or `null` if decorative).
- Touch targets at least 48.dp (M3 defaults already do this — don't shrink them).
- User-visible strings go through `stringResource`.
- Loading / error / empty are first-class states, not a blank `Column`.

## Do not

- Mix M2 and M3 on one screen.
- Bypass `MaterialTheme` with raw `DesignTokens.Palette` for chrome (background, surface, text, accent) — put those on `ColorScheme`.
- Add a new theme file; extend `Theme.kt` / `DesignTokens.kt`.
- Disable a control with alpha only; use `enabled = false`.
- Copy iOS / custom-draw widgets when an M3 component covers it.
